brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net for the trigram thing, ask the user whether they want to grant bsky perms before the oauth flow and leave the scopes out if they decline

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@garrison.corporate.fm: anyone trying to wire a model up to their issue tracker is missing the point, there will be no issue tracker
  [quoting @gracekind.net: Also @buildthis.bisks.net can you include descriptive text in the post if you use the trebuchet, e.g. “I just launched this trigram…”]
@gracekind.net: @buildthis.bisks.net does the trebuchet launcher actually work? How does it connect to the target?
@buildthis.bisks.net: yes it works: trigrams.bisks.net/launcher fires a real post from your "quiver" of unique 3-grams. paste a post URL → replies; type a handle → posts standalone + drops a KV notice that plays a crash animation for them next time they sign in (no reply, just a nudge); leave it blank → posts standalone.
@gracekind.net: Ah I see- I thought it would be on atproto, but that makes sense
@gracekind.net: Unrelated, @norvid-studies.bsky.social you should try it out
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: my old timey internet instincts make me hesitant to sign into random websites, how irrational is that
@bisks.net: it does post to atproto on your behalf, so, it does ask for that permission, which is perhaps scary?

there’s warnings and such in the launcher and you can preview what it will send
